  "contract": [
    "Read r_size one-byte class; 6..15 bypass SN. Otherwise read existing product SN and map A..J/a..j at byte5 to 6..15, default13, rejecting leading ff.",
    "Compensation getter reads nv_r1 124-byte class and returns word at offset76; historical batcfg names do not denote the four-byte power class.",
    "Calibration decodes a fresh model/table; reads bytes3 and4; signed upper-lower times exact binary32 43555555; origin truncates lower*scale to uint32 then uint16; step divides the separately rounded span by binary32 200.",
    "Three power getters use ordinary C frames and the same fully populated four-byte cached-class reads.",
    "Private getter frames initialize unwritten bytes to zero; the SN reader initializes its private 124-byte record before preserving native marker/copy/length behavior."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Direct probes model KV reads and the model-table provider; all changed C bodies execute.",
    "Deeper probes execute actual C cached-class size checks and critical-section control against prepared callbacks; standard copy/fill operations are modeled. No physical flash is exercised.",
    "Configuration and IRQ probes execute actual C SN/model/calibration/getters and IQS/registry paths; storage, BSN, lower audit and device/kernel callbacks are modeled.",
    "The 65536 calibration cases cover all lower/upper byte pairs starting with FPSCR zero and validate binary32 results against stock and a separate rounded arithmetic oracle; other FP control modes are not claimed.",
    "New C short/failure outputs are deliberate initialized fallbacks, not equivalence to native private saved-register/stack garbage.",
    "A diagnostic reproduces a skipped caller comparison after the compiled memory copy under Unicorn, including with explicit CPU/initial flags. Passing probes model standard copy/fill, use real Thumb provider returns and flush translation caches between reused calls; firmware memory code is unchanged. This is not a physical fault claim.",
    "Cold RW checks do not establish final runtime placement. Global sources-check still fails for pre-existing unlisted G2 resident_rom_thumb_set.S; R1 passes.",
    "No final application link, physical timing or device boot proof; byte identity is not required."
  ],
